# Copy to a file of your own and `source` it before scripts/design/music.sh, or set
# these inline. Only the first three have no default.
#
#   set -a; . scripts/design/music.env.example; set +a; scripts/design/music.sh
#
# Commented lines are the reference run's values. Uncommenting one at a different
# value changes the experiment, not just the run. The web-dev arm has its own file
# rather than a section here, because the two arms disagree on several of these
# names -- a shared file would let the wrong arm's value win silently.

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Policy checkpoint. HF layout or a Megatron-converted directory.
MODEL_PATH=/path/to/policy-checkpoint
# Build these first:
#   MUSIC_DATA=/path/to/music python3 -m recipes.design.music.build_parquet
TRAIN_DATA=/path/to/music_train.parquet
VAL_DATA=/path/to/music_val.parquet

# --- the one non-Python dependency ------------------------------------------
# The scorer shells out to `abc2midi`. Without it every sample skips, and a skip
# is reported as 0.0 -- so a whole run trains on all-zero rewards and looks
# healthy. run_music.sh probes for it on a worker and refuses to launch, printing
# `[probe] passed` when the check succeeds. Install the `abcmidi` package in the
# image, or point here:
# ABC2MIDI_BIN=/path/to/abc2midi

# --- cluster ----------------------------------------------------------------
# TRAIN_NNODES=8
# TRAIN_NGPUS_PER_NODE=8
# ACTOR_TP=8
# ACTOR_PP=1
# 1, not a tunable: sharding context over this model's linear attention layers is
# unexercised upstream.
# ACTOR_CP=1
# ROLLOUT_TP=4

# --- rollout ----------------------------------------------------------------
# ABC scores run long, so nearly the whole window is response budget:
# 116384 - 16384 = 100000 tokens for the score itself.
# MAXLEN=116384
# PROMPT_LENGTH=16384
# N=8
# TRAIN_BATCH_SIZE=32
# PPO_MINI_BATCH_SIZE=32
# TOTAL_EPOCHS=4
# ROLLOUT_GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85
# ROLLOUT_MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS=128
# verl spawns this many rollout worker actors, and a single-turn arm uses them
# too. verl's own default is 8, which is a quarter of this.
# AGENT_NUM_WORKERS=32
#
# Deliberately absent: sampling temperature, top-p and top-k. The reference run
# left verl's defaults in place, so naming them here at any value -- including one
# copied from another arm -- changes what this arm samples.

# --- scoring and identity ---------------------------------------------------
# Scoring is CPU-only and off the GPU critical path.
# REWARD_NUM_WORKERS=16
# This scorer has an absolute scale, unlike the web-dev arm's group-relative
# reward, so periodic validation is a number worth reading.
# TEST_FREQ=10
# SAVE_FREQ=10
# PROJECT_NAME=opensource-design
# EXP_NAME=music
